I couldn’t find “Record Rock Pro” anywhere in either file, so I read your request as “what’s missing to make the records feature solid and professional, especially the expanded card”. I went through the card code in dashboard.html and the /api/fetch-tab-records endpoint in server.js.

Fix first (correctness and security)

Missing access check: fetch-tab-records and mark-record-viewed never call userHasProjectAccess, though other endpoints like download-record-bundle do. Any logged-in user who knows a projectId could read that project’s records.
Unprotected file links: the “Signed notice (PDF)” button and the supporting-file links use the raw file_path/url as a plain href. The main document goes through previewRecordFile and downloadFile with auth. Given your earlier Cloudinary restrictions, these links will behave differently and aren’t protected.
Dead chevron: once a card is expanded, focusBottomCard marks it focused and the header click returns early. The chevron flips to ▴ but does nothing, and the only way out is “← Back to list”.
Missing in the expanded card

Unused data: the server sends stamp_type, stamp_status, stamped_doc_url, signature_hash, signed_by_display_name, notice_source and tied_record_title, and the dashboard never uses any of them. So there is no “Signed by X on date”, no stamp or verification status, and no “this notice relates to record Y”.
File details: .rc-file-sub is styled but never rendered, so the document row shows only a filename, with no size, type, page count or uploader.
Deadline: respond_by appears only inside notices. It should be a chip in the header, red when overdue.
Revision chain: “Superseded by #id” is plain text. Make it clickable, and add “Previous revision #x” on resubmissions.
Print and export: there is no @media print rule and no “export record summary (PDF)”. For contract records this is the most useful addition.
Keyboard and links: Escape and browser Back don’t return to the list, and there’s no copy-link or deep link to one record. The card also lacks aria-controls and doesn’t move focus into the detail.
Timeline: there is no single chronological activity log (uploaded → opened → signed → query raised → signer replaced → notice issued). Currently this is spread across the stepper, signers and “Activity”.
Backend

Audit trail: delete-record hard-deletes the record, its reviews and its notifications with no audit row. Only meetings have audit columns, so records need a record_events table, or a soft delete.
Performance: fetch-tab-records runs about 5 queries per record with no pagination, and the frontend renders every card at once. This will get slow as records grow.
Other tabs: Work Center, Planning & Execution, Document Approval and Control Reports each replace toggleRecordDetail with their own detail panels. I didn’t read those renderers, but they skip the focus mode and aria-expanded handling, so check they match the main card.
