Who can view and who can act (server.js)

Viewing: fetch-tab-records and mark-record-viewed now refuse anyone not assigned to the project. Before, any logged-in user who knew a projectId could read its records.
File downloads: download-file fetched any record’s file by id with no project check. It now checks the project the record belongs to. It also serves supporting files through the same checked route, with a new supportingIndex parameter.
Signing: review-record had a hole. A request could send actorType: 'team_member' and act as a team member even if the login token wasn’t a team member. It now requires a real team-member login, and also checks project access.
